WEBVTT

00:00:01.230 --> 00:00:04.980
"If the cuckoo won't sing,
I'll make it sing."

00:00:08.150 --> 00:00:10.400
Sakura, do you know that poem?

00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:13.070
Sure I do.

00:00:13.070 --> 00:00:14.990
From the cuckoo poems that were written

00:00:14.990 --> 00:00:17.620
to describe the personalities of
the Three Great Unifiers, right?

00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:20.330
"I'll make it sing" was Hideyoshi, wasn't it?

00:00:20.790 --> 00:00:22.460
But what brought this up?

00:00:27.330 --> 00:00:28.960
They already know about them...

00:00:29.380 --> 00:00:30.800
Hey, you guys!

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:33.840
Karin just learned that today,
and she was really impressed!

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:35.630
Try to read the mood!

00:02:07.180 --> 00:02:10.770
"If the cuckoo won't sing, I'll kill it."

00:02:11.440 --> 00:02:14.860
"If the cuckoo won't sing,
I'll make it sing."

00:02:15.730 --> 00:02:19.280
"If the cuckoo won't sing,
I'll wait until it sings."

00:02:21.570 --> 00:02:22.990
From these poems,

00:02:22.990 --> 00:02:25.240
we can determine that Nobunaga was crazy,

00:02:25.240 --> 00:02:27.580
Hideyoshi was normal and boring,

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:31.540
and Ieyasu was lazy.

00:02:32.290 --> 00:02:35.050
It's not like they composed
the poems themselves...

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:45.640
The subject just came up in class today.

00:02:46.100 --> 00:02:50.350
What? But doesn't first year Social
Studies only cover world history?

00:02:50.350 --> 00:02:52.480
Why were you talking about
generals of the Warring States?

00:02:52.980 --> 00:02:56.280
No, it wasn't in Social
Studies. It was in Math.

00:02:57.360 --> 00:02:58.860
That happens a lot.

00:02:59.450 --> 00:03:02.160
Maybe the teacher's original ambition

00:03:02.160 --> 00:03:04.450
to go into humanities showed up there.

00:03:05.330 --> 00:03:07.580
I guess he made a bit of a life mistake.

00:03:07.790 --> 00:03:08.790
Huh?!

00:03:09.910 --> 00:03:11.710
That happens a lot.

00:03:12.080 --> 00:03:15.170
But I was really impressed.

00:03:15.880 --> 00:03:18.170
I thought, if all the generals
had poems like that,

00:03:18.170 --> 00:03:21.720
it'd be easier for someone who's bad
at history to memorize things.

00:03:23.300 --> 00:03:26.180
I see! Then, I'll come up with one for you!

00:03:26.680 --> 00:03:30.940
"The cuckoo looks good in an eye patch."

00:03:32.480 --> 00:03:34.730
From this poem, you can determine

00:03:34.730 --> 00:03:37.520
that Masamune really loved eye patches.

00:03:37.520 --> 00:03:39.940
Masamune loved himself, then!

00:03:39.940 --> 00:03:41.570
Also, that's a little too random!

00:03:42.280 --> 00:03:44.700
I bet Masamune wouldn't take any damage

00:03:44.700 --> 00:03:47.120
unless his eye patch was destroyed first.

00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:48.450
What are you talking about?!

00:03:51.870 --> 00:03:53.710
You don't have to take notes!

00:03:53.710 --> 00:03:54.750
Hey, yeah!

00:03:54.750 --> 00:03:57.960
Now I can take Geography next year
instead of Japanese History.

00:03:57.960 --> 00:03:59.210
That's not the answer!

00:03:59.210 --> 00:04:01.010
That info won't help you,
even in Japanese History!

00:04:02.050 --> 00:04:02.510
One-Eyed Seal

00:04:02.510 --> 00:04:03.680
I'm Date!

00:04:05.220 --> 00:04:08.680
By the way, what would you do
in that situation, Karin?

00:04:08.680 --> 00:04:10.560
What? In what situation?

00:04:11.270 --> 00:04:13.810
You just got a cuckoo, but it won't sing.

00:04:13.810 --> 00:04:16.310
What would you do?

00:04:18.730 --> 00:04:20.900
Let me see...

00:04:21.570 --> 00:04:23.650
If the cuckoo won't sing...

00:04:25.030 --> 00:04:29.330
I-I have to take it to a hospital
because it might be sick!

00:04:34.500 --> 00:04:36.000
What?!

00:04:37.630 --> 00:04:39.460
I want you to be my little sister.

00:04:39.460 --> 00:04:41.670
Why do your eyes look so serious?!

00:04:41.670 --> 00:04:42.800
Because I mean it.

00:04:42.800 --> 00:04:44.260
You meant that?!

00:04:44.260 --> 00:04:46.970
Then, what would you do, Natsuki?

00:04:46.970 --> 00:04:49.010
What? Me?

00:04:51.060 --> 00:04:54.640
Uh, let me see...

00:04:56.190 --> 00:05:00.360
If the cuckoo won't sing,
I guess I'm okay with that.

00:05:00.360 --> 00:05:02.360
I see!

00:05:02.360 --> 00:05:03.650
Don't entertain lofty ambitions,

00:05:03.650 --> 00:05:06.030
but accept the situation for what it is,

00:05:06.030 --> 00:05:07.780
and try to enjoy it.

00:05:08.280 --> 00:05:11.120
This poem embodies the
spirit of modern youth.

00:05:11.120 --> 00:05:13.370
You don't have to analyze it that much...

00:05:13.790 --> 00:05:18.040
I'm just not that interested
in listening to cuckoos singing.

00:05:18.380 --> 00:05:19.670
You modern youth, you!

00:05:19.670 --> 00:05:22.300
What would you do, then, Sakura?

00:05:24.260 --> 00:05:25.840
Let me see...

00:05:25.840 --> 00:05:27.430
I figure the cuckoo

00:05:27.430 --> 00:05:32.060
probably has its own reasons
for not singing... So I'd say...

00:05:34.520 --> 00:05:38.770
If the cuckoo won't sing,
try smiling instead.

00:05:38.770 --> 00:05:40.440
That's not kindness!

00:05:40.440 --> 00:05:42.900
You're putting even more pressure on it!

00:05:44.440 --> 00:05:47.700
I'm pretty much the same as Ieyasu.

00:05:47.700 --> 00:05:50.320
You mean you'd wait until it sings?

00:05:50.780 --> 00:05:51.950
Yeah.

00:05:52.790 --> 00:05:57.210
If the cuckoo won't sing,
I'll wait until it sings.

00:05:57.660 --> 00:06:00.420
Until its tears turn into stars in the sky!

00:06:00.420 --> 00:06:02.630
She added a lower phrase!

00:06:02.630 --> 00:06:05.960
I'm pretty sure Ieyasu wasn't
that much of a romantic!

00:06:06.630 --> 00:06:08.470
It's because, back in middle school,

00:06:08.470 --> 00:06:10.970
I was the type who'd write lyrics
without music to go with them.

00:06:11.550 --> 00:06:14.140
Why did you just confess to that?

00:06:14.600 --> 00:06:15.970
What about you, Claire?

00:06:15.970 --> 00:06:18.600
Let's see... To be honest,

00:06:18.600 --> 00:06:21.690
I don't fully understand
what these poems mean.

00:06:21.690 --> 00:06:23.820
Huh? You don't understand them?

00:06:23.820 --> 00:06:25.650
Well, you know...

00:06:26.150 --> 00:06:30.160
If the cuckoo won't sing,
why not just get a canary?

00:06:33.080 --> 00:06:35.290
That's not the issue!

00:06:36.830 --> 00:06:40.370
Um... I know it's a little late to ask this, but...

00:06:40.620 --> 00:06:43.540
What type of bird is a cuckoo?

00:06:44.960 --> 00:06:46.670
Good question. What kind of bird is it?

00:06:46.670 --> 00:06:49.970
Um... I think it's... green, and...

00:06:49.970 --> 00:06:51.550
That's a bush warbler.

00:06:51.840 --> 00:06:55.470
I think it's yellow, and
used as a dyeing agent...

00:06:55.470 --> 00:06:57.680
I think you're describing sodium chromate.

00:06:57.680 --> 00:06:59.730
How did you get those confused?!

00:06:59.730 --> 00:07:02.860
It's a type of bird: small, medium,

00:07:02.860 --> 00:07:05.650
or possibly large, with
two wings it uses to fly.

00:07:06.020 --> 00:07:07.730
It also has a beak.

00:07:07.730 --> 00:07:10.700
Oh, it's that kind of bird.

00:07:10.700 --> 00:07:11.950
Use your head, Karin!

00:07:11.950 --> 00:07:14.030
That applies to most birds!

00:07:14.450 --> 00:07:16.740
Also, the females lay eggs.

00:07:16.740 --> 00:07:18.500
Only the females, not the males.

00:07:18.790 --> 00:07:20.580
You can stop giving that kind of info!

00:07:20.580 --> 00:07:22.540
It's not helping the description at all!

00:07:22.880 --> 00:07:24.460
But it's strange, isn't it?

00:07:24.460 --> 00:07:26.880
We've been saying all these things,

00:07:26.880 --> 00:07:29.920
but none of us actually
knows what a cuckoo is.

00:07:31.340 --> 00:07:33.430
Maybe, instead of a cuckoo bird, it's...

00:07:37.890 --> 00:07:39.310
She's not really...

00:07:42.020 --> 00:07:43.440
...going to say it, is she?

00:07:48.780 --> 00:07:50.190
...a bird <i>gone</i> cuckoo!

00:07:50.490 --> 00:07:52.530
She said it!

00:07:54.110 --> 00:07:56.240
There are some jokes you know are bad,

00:07:56.240 --> 00:07:58.450
but you just have to say them anyway!

00:08:07.290 --> 00:08:10.050
I brought cookies today!

00:08:10.340 --> 00:08:12.050
Yay!

00:08:18.720 --> 00:08:20.470
Oh, they're good!

00:08:20.470 --> 00:08:22.230
Where did you buy them?

00:08:22.600 --> 00:08:24.230
Don't say that, Sakura.

00:08:24.600 --> 00:08:26.730
I made them myself!

00:08:29.320 --> 00:08:31.150
You fiend! Who are you?!

00:08:32.780 --> 00:08:34.950
Huh? What?!

00:08:40.950 --> 00:08:42.040
Wait a minute!

00:08:42.540 --> 00:08:45.920
You mean Karin isn't the
"brainless beauty" archetype?

00:08:47.290 --> 00:08:49.420
I figured, if she tried to cook...

00:08:50.880 --> 00:08:53.420
She'd be the type to make the pot explode!

00:08:53.420 --> 00:08:57.680
Please, Sakura. Food doesn't explode.

00:08:57.680 --> 00:08:59.510
You are correct!

00:09:00.010 --> 00:09:02.520
Oh no! I've got "anime brain"!

00:09:02.810 --> 00:09:08.440
Oh, but... eggs do explode
if you microwave them,

00:09:08.440 --> 00:09:10.020
so you have to be careful.

00:09:10.860 --> 00:09:13.030
You even went to the trouble
of naming an exception!

00:09:13.240 --> 00:09:14.490
What is this feeling?

00:09:14.490 --> 00:09:16.780
I suddenly want to wrap her in kindness...

00:09:17.160 --> 00:09:20.330
I didn't know Karin had a talent like that.

00:09:20.330 --> 00:09:22.120
Did you know, Natsuki?

00:09:22.120 --> 00:09:25.290
Nope. This is the first I've heard of it, too.

00:09:26.120 --> 00:09:27.790
Feminine Appeal: 5,000!

00:09:28.130 --> 00:09:29.040
Impossible!

00:09:29.500 --> 00:09:31.380
From an Earthling?!

00:09:31.380 --> 00:09:33.260
Where did you pull that thing from?!

00:09:33.260 --> 00:09:34.630
Is the device malfunctioning?!

00:09:34.630 --> 00:09:36.840
I think your brain is malfunctioning!

00:09:37.090 --> 00:09:41.310
I was actually in the Home
Ec Club in middle school.

00:09:41.310 --> 00:09:43.770
I'm good at cooking and sewing.

00:09:43.770 --> 00:09:45.770
Oh, really?

00:09:45.770 --> 00:09:49.150
So why didn't you join the
Home Ec Club in high school?

00:09:49.150 --> 00:09:50.980
It's because this school separates it

00:09:50.980 --> 00:09:53.440
into Cooking Club and Handicrafts Club.

00:09:54.030 --> 00:09:57.740
And while I was trying
to pick between them,

00:09:58.490 --> 00:10:00.120
that's when I found the Going Home Club!

00:10:00.570 --> 00:10:01.780
How did you decide on this club

00:10:01.780 --> 00:10:04.660
as a happy medium between the two?

00:10:05.200 --> 00:10:07.870
It's impressive that you can sew, too.

00:10:07.870 --> 00:10:10.080
I'd love to see something you've made.

00:10:10.080 --> 00:10:11.290
In that case...

00:10:13.050 --> 00:10:15.260
This tissue cover is handmade!

00:10:15.710 --> 00:10:19.550
N-Not only does she put a cover
on her pocket tissues...

00:10:19.550 --> 00:10:21.260
...but it's handmade, too?!

00:10:21.640 --> 00:10:23.140
Feminine Appeal Level: 40,000...

00:10:23.720 --> 00:10:24.890
50,000...

00:10:25.390 --> 00:10:26.930
It's still rising!

00:10:27.480 --> 00:10:30.480
Seriously, where did you buy that thing?

00:10:30.850 --> 00:10:34.730
Karin must be of a race that can
alter its Feminine Appeal at will.

00:10:34.730 --> 00:10:36.530
She's joined in, too!

00:10:37.190 --> 00:10:39.400
What formidable Feminine Appeal!

00:10:42.200 --> 00:10:44.620
To bring me of all people to my knees...

00:10:44.620 --> 00:10:46.290
Why are you on your knees?!

00:10:48.210 --> 00:10:50.370
Truth is...

00:10:52.080 --> 00:10:54.000
I've heard of this.

00:10:57.920 --> 00:11:01.510
They say that any girl
can become a princess!

00:11:04.180 --> 00:11:06.060
You mean that Karin...

00:11:06.060 --> 00:11:08.100
has another transformation coming up?!

00:11:11.190 --> 00:11:13.020
It exploded!

00:11:13.520 --> 00:11:16.270
A device that explodes when it
exceeds its measuring parameters

00:11:16.270 --> 00:11:18.280
goes against the PL Law!

00:11:25.370 --> 00:11:28.040
How did you end up like that?!

00:11:29.500 --> 00:11:31.000
I can't win...

00:11:31.000 --> 00:11:32.960
What are you even fighting?!

00:11:32.960 --> 00:11:37.250
By the way, the PL Law refers
to the Product Liability Law,

00:11:37.250 --> 00:11:40.760
a regulation prohibiting the
sale of dangerous goods.

00:11:41.260 --> 00:11:42.680
She gave an explanation!

00:11:42.680 --> 00:11:47.930
Also... it has nothing to do...
with high school... baseball...

00:11:50.730 --> 00:11:53.520
I... I'm done for, too...

00:11:53.520 --> 00:11:54.520
Why?!

00:11:54.520 --> 00:11:57.110
This... atmosphere...

00:12:03.280 --> 00:12:05.870
These people take a mood way too far!

00:12:06.200 --> 00:12:08.290
Seriously, what is happening here?!

00:12:10.080 --> 00:12:12.330
I don't really get it, but...

00:12:14.330 --> 00:12:16.330
They liked the stuff I made!

00:12:29.390 --> 00:12:30.720
Hello.

00:12:31.060 --> 00:12:32.980
Oh, the new recruits are here.

00:12:32.980 --> 00:12:33.980
Yes!

00:12:47.910 --> 00:12:49.740
Botan, listen to this!

00:12:51.450 --> 00:12:52.750
What is it?

00:12:53.290 --> 00:12:55.420
A girl who was in my class in middle school

00:12:55.420 --> 00:12:57.500
said she went to a social mixer recently!

00:12:58.040 --> 00:12:59.750
High school girls are too young for that!

00:13:02.260 --> 00:13:03.550
I agree!

00:13:11.520 --> 00:13:12.770
This is good.

00:13:15.060 --> 00:13:16.270
What?

00:13:22.360 --> 00:13:25.610
A social mixer isn't that unusual, is it?

00:13:25.610 --> 00:13:27.740
It was normal at my middle school.

00:13:27.740 --> 00:13:29.780
What kind of middle school did you go to?!

00:13:30.530 --> 00:13:31.910
Excuse me...

00:13:32.370 --> 00:13:34.330
but what is a social mixer?

00:13:34.330 --> 00:13:36.670
I don't know anything about them.

00:13:36.920 --> 00:13:38.170
Let me explain!

00:13:38.920 --> 00:13:41.750
A social mixer is an event in
which several boys and girls

00:13:41.750 --> 00:13:44.300
work together toward a common goal,

00:13:44.300 --> 00:13:46.170
occasionally clashing, as they

00:13:46.170 --> 00:13:49.140
grow up and improve one another.

00:13:49.140 --> 00:13:51.180
Is it really something that noble?

00:13:51.760 --> 00:13:53.520
Incidentally,

00:13:54.310 --> 00:13:56.350
in my third year of middle school,
we sang Die Moldau.

00:13:57.100 --> 00:14:00.150
Oh... I was hoping I was wrong...

00:14:00.860 --> 00:14:02.860
but you're thinking of a <i>choral</i> mixer.

00:14:03.610 --> 00:14:04.440
What?

00:14:06.700 --> 00:14:09.700
No, oh no... You're talking
about the <i>other</i> kind?!

00:14:09.700 --> 00:14:11.160
She really mixed them up?

00:14:11.160 --> 00:14:13.200
She's surprisingly innocent!

00:14:13.370 --> 00:14:14.910
A social mixer

00:14:14.910 --> 00:14:19.460
is a lowbrow event where outgoing men
and women who've never met before

00:14:19.460 --> 00:14:22.500
come together to get better
acquainted, with the goal of dating.

00:14:22.920 --> 00:14:25.210
Oh, I see.

00:14:26.210 --> 00:14:28.760
But you know, we <i>are</i> already in high school!

00:14:29.180 --> 00:14:32.470
A social mixer could break out at any time,

00:14:32.470 --> 00:14:34.060
and we could get caught up in it!

00:14:34.310 --> 00:14:37.730
Okay! Today, we're going to do
a social mixer practice drill!

00:14:38.100 --> 00:14:41.560
Are social mixers like natural disasters now?!

00:14:43.110 --> 00:14:46.780
And so, playing along with
Sakura's idea,

00:14:47.150 --> 00:14:51.030
we all drew lots to determine our roles.

00:14:52.950 --> 00:14:54.580
What do you mean, the referee?!

00:14:54.580 --> 00:14:56.240
Does a social mixer need one of those?

00:14:57.080 --> 00:15:01.040
I'll be judging your social mixer etiquette.

00:15:01.790 --> 00:15:04.790
But she doesn't have any experience
with social mixers either...

00:15:05.460 --> 00:15:07.960
Okay! Social mixer, start!

00:15:09.970 --> 00:15:11.970
Saying "Start" doesn't help us much...

00:15:11.970 --> 00:15:16.600
Um... since we're supposed to
be people who've never met,

00:15:16.600 --> 00:15:18.980
maybe we should introduce ourselves?

00:15:19.310 --> 00:15:22.020
Great job! +10 to Botan!

00:15:22.020 --> 00:15:23.980
You're scoring <i>that</i>?!

00:15:24.690 --> 00:15:26.440
My name is Oohagi Botan.

00:15:26.900 --> 00:15:28.490
My special skill is earth splitting.

00:15:29.150 --> 00:15:31.110
By earth splitting, you mean...

00:15:42.120 --> 00:15:44.380
No, not that.

00:15:54.390 --> 00:15:56.260
You didn't mean earthenware?!

00:15:56.550 --> 00:15:58.890
My name is Kokonoe Claire.

00:15:58.890 --> 00:16:01.560
I play a bit of Stradivarius.

00:16:01.560 --> 00:16:03.560
Why don't you just say "violin"?!

00:16:03.560 --> 00:16:05.520
I also do tea ceremonies from time to time.

00:16:08.190 --> 00:16:10.940
Yohen Tenmoku tea bowls are national treasures!

00:16:10.940 --> 00:16:13.780
Why do you always call attention to the
fact that you're on a different plane?

00:16:15.570 --> 00:16:16.830
Well, I'm...

00:16:16.830 --> 00:16:18.910
I've brought you some wasabi octopus!

00:16:19.240 --> 00:16:22.620
Right now?! Read the atmosphere, waitress!

00:16:22.620 --> 00:16:26.460
If you need anything,
please press the button.

00:16:26.460 --> 00:16:29.130
Why is that part so realistic?!

00:16:29.380 --> 00:16:31.550
What's wasabi octopus?

00:16:33.380 --> 00:16:37.510
Once again, I'm Andou
Natsuki. My hobby is...

00:16:42.390 --> 00:16:44.890
making felt dolls.

00:16:46.230 --> 00:16:48.060
What was I supposed to say?!

00:16:50.030 --> 00:16:51.650
I'm Touno Karin.

00:16:52.280 --> 00:16:55.700
Lately, I enjoy floral-scented baths.

00:16:56.610 --> 00:17:00.910
I'm not very good at studying,
but my favorite tea is darjeeling.

00:17:01.700 --> 00:17:03.830
She got a high score for that?

00:17:03.830 --> 00:17:05.920
But I didn't even understand
that last thing she said!

00:17:06.960 --> 00:17:08.670
By the way, did you know?

00:17:08.670 --> 00:17:12.760
In flower language, the Cosmos flower
represents "a maiden's devotion."

00:17:13.630 --> 00:17:14.550
What?!

00:17:14.550 --> 00:17:17.220
Her Feminine Appeal Level is beyond measure.

00:17:17.220 --> 00:17:20.060
What? You're still dragging up that joke?

00:17:20.970 --> 00:17:22.310
Rain seal.

00:17:22.970 --> 00:17:25.560
Well, we finished our introductions.

00:17:25.850 --> 00:17:27.810
So now...

00:17:28.190 --> 00:17:30.020
...what are we...

00:17:30.520 --> 00:17:32.030
...supposed to do?

00:17:36.740 --> 00:17:39.070
I brought more wasabi octopus!

00:17:39.410 --> 00:17:42.120
A second wasabi octopus onslaught?!

00:17:42.120 --> 00:17:44.700
How desperate is this store to
push the wasabi octopus?!

00:17:44.700 --> 00:17:49.500
Well, wasabi octopus is
the only bar snack I know.

00:17:49.500 --> 00:17:52.090
There's a lot of options! Like fried foods!

00:17:52.090 --> 00:17:53.840
I didn't think of that!

00:17:53.840 --> 00:17:56.590
Time for a freebie!

00:17:57.050 --> 00:17:58.130
Huh?

00:17:58.130 --> 00:18:00.850
If you bring up the next topic
smoothly, you get a high score!

00:18:00.850 --> 00:18:03.100
Make it clear if you're the
waitress or the referee!

00:18:05.060 --> 00:18:08.730
You both have such lovely outfits.

00:18:08.730 --> 00:18:11.110
Where do you usually go shopping?

00:18:11.520 --> 00:18:13.940
That's an incredibly high score!

00:18:13.940 --> 00:18:16.030
Your scoring standards make no sense!

00:18:17.860 --> 00:18:21.660
That kind of inflation makes
this feel like a real battle!

00:18:21.660 --> 00:18:23.870
Why does that make her so excited?!

00:18:23.870 --> 00:18:26.120
Besides, this isn't even a battle!

00:18:26.500 --> 00:18:32.000
I usually shop locally, but
sometimes I go to Harajuku, too!

00:18:32.380 --> 00:18:34.630
Oh, really.

00:18:39.720 --> 00:18:41.800
That topic didn't go as far as expected...

00:18:42.760 --> 00:18:45.640
I brought some fried wasabi octopus!

00:18:45.970 --> 00:18:48.770
Why are you so insistent on wasabi octopus?!

00:18:48.770 --> 00:18:50.520
Just bring over some ordinary chicken!

00:18:50.520 --> 00:18:52.480
Oh, I see. That'll work.

00:18:53.610 --> 00:18:56.150
Time for an unexpected incident!

00:18:56.610 --> 00:18:59.780
Botan spills a drink and loses points!

00:18:59.780 --> 00:19:03.160
What? Random events happen in this, too?

00:19:04.160 --> 00:19:06.160
What an explosive drop!

00:19:06.410 --> 00:19:07.790
Interesting!

00:19:07.790 --> 00:19:10.420
She gets more excited
the more digits are added!

00:19:10.420 --> 00:19:11.670
She's so easy to read!

00:19:11.920 --> 00:19:14.420
I've brought some fried chicken!

00:19:14.880 --> 00:19:18.170
Oh, finally. A proper dish.

00:19:19.920 --> 00:19:22.010
Put lemon on the fried chicken?

00:19:23.340 --> 00:19:26.310
Um... I'll choose "Yes."

00:19:28.470 --> 00:19:30.520
The lemon has revealed its true form!

00:19:30.770 --> 00:19:34.690
You look closely and see it's not
a lemon after all, but a durian!

00:19:34.690 --> 00:19:36.270
Will this result in a huge drop of score?!

00:19:36.270 --> 00:19:37.650
What kind of situation is this?!

00:19:38.900 --> 00:19:40.150
I want to see the manager.

00:19:44.530 --> 00:19:47.080
She jumped back into the lead with a complaint!

00:19:48.290 --> 00:19:50.290
Social mixers are a complicated thing.

00:19:50.290 --> 00:19:52.170
You're just making it up as you go!

00:19:52.540 --> 00:19:53.460
Blub blub?

00:19:54.210 --> 00:19:56.250
It's time to wrap it up!

00:19:58.210 --> 00:20:02.590
I'm not sure what's going on,
but I'd like to take Karin out.

00:20:02.590 --> 00:20:03.470
Okay!

00:20:03.470 --> 00:20:05.850
She's become quite the carnivore.

00:20:07.100 --> 00:20:09.520
How long do you want
your takeout to keep?

00:20:09.520 --> 00:20:11.480
Don't try to preserve her with dry ice!

00:20:11.480 --> 00:20:13.310
Coming through! Coming through!

00:20:13.310 --> 00:20:15.860
Now that you've chosen the
one you'd like to take out,

00:20:15.860 --> 00:20:18.440
I will announce the final scores!

00:20:23.860 --> 00:20:25.910
The winner is... Karin!

00:20:26.450 --> 00:20:27.870
Hooray?

00:20:28.870 --> 00:20:32.540
I bestow upon Karin the
title of "Social Mixer Goddess!"

00:20:33.250 --> 00:20:34.710
Yay?

00:20:35.960 --> 00:20:37.130
All right!

00:20:37.130 --> 00:20:40.340
Now you'll all know what to do if
you're ever caught up in a social mixer.

00:20:40.760 --> 00:20:41.970
Miss Waitress.

00:20:43.010 --> 00:20:45.890
When do you get off work?

00:20:50.970 --> 00:20:53.560
Hey! You can't make a pass at the waitress!

00:22:25.860 --> 00:22:27.240
Sakura.

00:22:28.490 --> 00:22:31.620
I was thinking about it,
and a chorus made up of boys

00:22:31.620 --> 00:22:34.200
and girls would be a mixed
chorus, not a choral mixer.

00:22:34.740 --> 00:22:37.500
You couldn't have confused
it with a social mixer.

00:22:40.000 --> 00:22:42.420
Mixed shock!

00:22:45.920 --> 00:22:46.920
Sakura here!

00:22:46.920 --> 00:22:49.300
I heard aye-ayes have extremely
long middle fingers

00:22:49.300 --> 00:22:52.180
that they use to pull
grubs out of tree trunks!

00:22:52.390 --> 00:22:54.310
Bet it's useful for picking their noses, too!

00:22:57.730 --> 00:23:00.020
And others, with a sandwich on the side!
